# assets/*.html are not application code -- they are the render sources the
# banner and avatar PNGs are generated from, kept in the repo so the images
# can be edited and reproduced rather than only replaced. Linguist should
# read them as documentation, not count them as part of the codebase.
assets/*.html linguist-documentation

# demo/ is a fixture-data mockup of the finished case file, not the running
# product. It stays in the repo because it shows the intended shape, but it
# is not what anyone should read to understand how thread works.
demo/* linguist-documentation
